{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915350-supernatural-enemies-that-make-good-crossover-antagonists","id":915350,"title":"Supernatural enemies that make good crossover antagonists?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-15T20:54:06-07:00","id":915350,"title":"Supernatural enemies that make good crossover antagonists?","content":"So, I've been thinking, any antagonists from certain lines that you think would make great baddies for other lines? Some examples-<br /> <br /> - Idigam vs. Promethean: Atamajakki had a great idea for a 1950s Promethean dark era based on 50s and 60s atomic horror b-movies, so why not pit them against The Thing From Outer Space- in this case, an Idigam that's causing bizarre mutations. Maybe it's even taken a liking to flux and the Centimani, and wants to transform into some kind of pseudo-Qashmallim? For bonus points, set it in either New Mexico or one of the poles. <br /> <br /> - Fae vs. Demons: Mysterious thorny growths have been cropping up over local Infrastructure, causing it to act strangely. The Ring might initially think this is a good thing- it's fucking with the GM- but then the damage to the infrastructure starts causing dangerous reality glitches. And then they find out that the GM's plan to solve the situation involves &quot;cauterizing the wound&quot; by setting off a massive natural disaster and razing entire city blocks to the ground. <br /> <br /> - Strix vs. Beasts: A well-intentioned Begotten &quot;patron&quot; of the local Kindred is seduced by a Stirge, who wants to use him to push the vampires into barbarism. What will the players think of this new threat- assuming they can detect it. And when they do, how will they react to an entity that claims to embody their guiding principles even more closely than they do?<br /> <br /> - Tremere Lich vs. Sin-Eaters: A very old and very powerful Lich is on a quest to refine his flawed immortality, and his resources have notified him of the existence of the Bargain. The possibilities are almost endless, but he's decided to start by hunting down as many Geists are possible and binding them to himself and his servants. If the Krewe has dealt with abmortals, they might be in for a surprise when they find out just how powerful this one is. <br /> <br /> - Pandoran vs. Sangiovanni: One of the most prominent, wealthiest, and skilled Sangiovanni, owner of a sprawling estate and laboratory complex, suddenly drops out of contact with the rest of the &quot;family&quot;. When the players are dispatched to investigate, they find out that their experiments on creating even more perfect undead servants have created a brood of Pandorans led by a Sublimati, who have claimed the estate as their own twisted lair. <br /> <br /> - Kerberos vs Mummies: Yet another Atamajakki-inspired hook. So, you can draw a lot of interesting parallels between Geist and Mummy, especially with the whole &quot;brought back to life and maintained by a minor god of death&quot; thing giving some interesting similarities between the Bargain and the Rite of Return. Mummies looking for some answers could likely end up in the underworld...only to find that its monstrous overlords don't take kindly to outsiders snooping around. Perhaps they'll even seek an audience with Polydegmon himself...what would he make of such venerable deathless beings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:09:51-07:00","id":915367,"title":"","content":"Vampires have to be absolutely terrifying to the Arisen. Sure, you can kill them easily enough... but an Elder has had all the time you've been in henet to scheme and leave nasty surprises for you. Fail to take care of one during a Descent, and they've possibly got centuries to conspire to keep you asleep and to subvert your Cult. <br /> <br /> I keep seeing arguments that Changelings get along well with Beasts, but it's for me to imagine anything more terrifying short of one of the Gentry themselves. Everyone else sees a normal person, but you see a walking, talking nightmare; are they blind, or is your Clarity starting to slip? When a living piece of the story starts stalking people and dragging them off to places that don't exist, things start to get uncomfortably familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:13:44-07:00","id":915371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915350-supernatural-enemies-that-make-good-crossover-antagonists?p=915367#post915367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep seeing arguments that Changelings get along well with Beasts, but it's for me to imagine anything more terrifying short of one of the Gentry themselves. Everyone else sees a normal person, but you see a walking, talking nightmare; are they blind, or is your Clarity starting to slip? When a living piece of the story starts stalking people and dragging them off to places that don't exist, things start to get uncomfortably familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what if the Beast in question decides it's more profitable to run with hunstmen than freeholders?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:20:47-07:00","id":915375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915350-supernatural-enemies-that-make-good-crossover-antagonists?p=915371#post915371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what if the Beast in question decides it's more profitable to run with hunstmen than freeholders?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I've always felt that Beast needed to address the very real possibility of this happening. <br /> <br /> And just imagine how Militias and Bridgeburners would react to them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:23:36-07:00","id":915376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915350-supernatural-enemies-that-make-good-crossover-antagonists?p=915367#post915367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone else sees a normal person, but you see a walking, talking nightmare; are they blind, or is your Clarity starting to slip?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Eshmaki neighbor needs to stop leaving his Atavisms on, is what's happening.<br /> <br /> I think an idigam would make for a nicely disquieting source of Mysteries for mages with an interest in the Shadow, between the host of dramatic changes they can evoke in the local Shadow, their complete immunity to binding powers, and the ease with which one can draw parallels between Obsession and spiritual monomania.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:28:23-07:00","id":915378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915350-supernatural-enemies-that-make-good-crossover-antagonists?p=915371#post915371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what if the Beast in question decides it's more profitable to run with hunstmen than freeholders?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who a Beast is really going to feel Kinship to, the broken mostly-human victims of the Fae or the proud lords and predators of Acradia, resplendent in their monstrous, otherworldly glory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:42:27-07:00","id":915387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915350-supernatural-enemies-that-make-good-crossover-antagonists?p=915378#post915378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who a Beast is really going to feel Kinship to, the broken mostly-human victims of the Fae or the proud lords and predators of Acradia, resplendent in their monstrous, otherworldly glory?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to put my money on the kids who have thwarted gods and made the local color their own over the ban-riddled aliens and the recurrent drones who are just in town for one job and have a finite quantity of diversionary targets, to be frank. Monsters is monsters, and monsters you share a background with are easier to get along with than a set of cousins who hardly ever call. Having a family get-together with landed Gentry is the domain of Apexes and other biggest-kids.<br /> <br /> <br /> Never mind the Kerberoi, I think the more curious strain of Arisen are going to be most like to demand to know exactly the fuck is going on in those cases where geister don't offer the full Bargain but still wind up sharing bits of a mortal soul with some poor sod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:44:44-07:00","id":915390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915350-supernatural-enemies-that-make-good-crossover-antagonists?p=915378#post915378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who a Beast is really going to feel Kinship to, the broken mostly-human victims of the Fae or the proud lords and predators of Acradia, resplendent in their monstrous, otherworldly glory?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't see a Beast coming out well from that, since if things get far enough along they'll have an entire Freehold mobilized against them. That is, unless they're subtle enough about it and hide their true alignment. <br /> <br /> When they get found out...Beasts probably end up with KOS status in that area among the Lost. <br /> <br /> This is where Beasts having more of a community could be helpful- so we have some source of &quot;quests&quot; to tell the players &quot;Hey, kill this Beast before the Changelings find out who he works for of our relationship to the Freehold is permanently fucked.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:53:49-07:00","id":915395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915350-supernatural-enemies-that-make-good-crossover-antagonists?p=915375#post915375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I've always felt that Beast needed to address the very real possibility of this happening.<br /> <br /> And just imagine how Militias and Bridgeburners would react to them...</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts really are more in-line with the standard antagonist groups. They're basically walking loci for fear spirits, their lessons fall in line with the sacred prey of the Pure, Tyrants and the hosts probably get along like best buddies. The book goes and says hostile mages might believe they're related to the Exarchs, and I personally think that they would get along better with the Seers than the Diamond. I always found it odd that they were pushed to the more usually played factions.<br /> <br /> Back to the topic, I think Claimed can really be a good antagonist for any line. They're powerful and monstrous but can be more subtle too.<br /> <br /> I tried using Pandorans once in a game, apparently mechanically they need a Promethean nearby or they go into torpor. It's an easy rule to throw out, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T23:15:21-07:00","id":915424,"title":"","content":"I've always felt that the best way to handle things in crossover is by using Hunter's example: Just take the vague concept and stat it however you want. Your players may never even know that mechanically your Vampire is using Spells because you don't want to bother remembering how Vampire works. Having Dread Powers in the corebook makes this all the easier. I once had <i>Kuchisake-Onna</i> show up in a game and because I don't like how the Slasher templates work, I gave her five dots of Physical Disciplines from Requiem 2e and I think two Numina.<br /> <br /> So don't limit yourself to directly using the things from other gamelines exactly. I feel like that's an easy mistake that gets made often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T23:48:18-07:00","id":915433,"title":"","content":"Thrysus mages of whatever variety seem like pretty good Werewolf villains, and a nice example of someone from the Flesh invading the Shadow to warp it to their agenda instead of the reverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11821-st-just","name":"St.Just","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T01:19:00-07:00","id":915458,"title":"","content":"The basic Arisen arc of starting impossibly powerful and single minded but growing weaker and more aware as time goes on could make for a really cool antagonist set up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T01:40:59-07:00","id":915464,"title":"","content":"I kind of have Leviathans replace Beasts in my personal ChroD, since you can't really fit them in together, but it would be fun to see how they'd interact. <br /> <br /> Imagine a School of Clay leviathan who's established a mostly benevolent &quot;cult&quot; around an oceanographic institute, which she mostly monitors and interacts with from afar to keep the Wake from messing with things. And then imagine some smug Makara starts attacking and setting traps for the institute's divers and researchers, claiming that he's &quot;teaching them a lesson about hubris&quot; or something like that.<br /> <br /> And pity the Beast who confuses Marduk agents for Heroes.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Leviathans, I imagine they'd get along either really well or really badly with the Brineborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 06-16-2016, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T04:10:52-07:00","id":915504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915350-supernatural-enemies-that-make-good-crossover-antagonists?p=915376#post915376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Eshmaki neighbor needs to stop leaving his Atavisms on, is what's happening.<br /> <br /> I think an idigam would make for a nicely disquieting source of Mysteries for mages with an interest in the Shadow, between the host of dramatic changes they can evoke in the local Shadow, their complete immunity to binding powers, and the ease with which one can draw parallels between Obsession and spiritual monomania.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note: Idigam are stated to being immune to attempts at controlling them, I believe the exact phrase was &quot;binding their will&quot;. Binding them is exactly what produced the Earthbound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T04:15:14-07:00","id":917937,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for fodder here, go look at the stuff from <b>Dragon, both 2nd and 3rd edition</b>: I've pulled Hydras and Deep Ones from those before, and there are a few other cool antagonists in there. <b>Hydras</b> being good for balls-out crazy-monster attacks and <b>Deep Ones</b> being good for that subtle &quot;is it evil or just creepy&quot; kind of monster. I also know that <b>Vampires</b> make for good fakeout-villains, and I tend to use them for that on alot of newer players, because they see Vampires running some massive conspiracy and don't know enough to realize that that's just status quo. I also enjoy tossing anything from Inferno in. Obviously, <b>Hunters are the best antagonists</b>, because they're probably the closest thing to a &quot;bad guy splat&quot; which was made with PCs in mind. If you want more, you should go look into a book called <b>Antagonists</b>. Also, look up the SCP Foundation for some great monsters.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, remember that all templates have their &quot;evil&quot; Y-Splat. Vampires have <b>Ballai's Brood </b>(and <b>Invictus</b>, who are less evil and more stuck in outdated ways), Werewolf has the <b>Pure</b> (3 unique kinds!) and <b>Bale Hounds</b>, and I pulled imagery from the <b>Black Spiral Dancers</b> into the campaign I ran when I first got my copy of 2nd edition, Mages have <b>Seers</b> and a few other nasty things... Every book mentions something.<br /> <br /> Also watch the stuff we're releasing for <b>Dragon Rekindled</b>. <b>The Deep Ones</b>, <b>Knights of the Bloody Chalice</b> (coming this week), <b>Nightmares</b>, and <b>Nihilists</b> are being written with Crossover in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}